<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
11. Section 210.39 is amended by redesignating paragraphs (b) through (d) as paragraphs (c) through (e) and adding
a new paragraph b to read as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;210.39 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
In camera treatment of confidential information. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * * 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Transmission of certain Commission records to district court.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 In a civil action involving parties that are also parties to a proceeding before the Commission under section 337 of
the Tariff Act of 1930, at the request of a party to the civil action that is also a respondent in the proceeding before
the Commission, the district court may stay, until the determination of the Commission becomes final, proceedings
in the civil action with respect to any claim that involves the same issues involved in the proceeding before the Commission
under certain conditions. If such a stay is in effect, after the determination of the Commission becomes final, the
Commission shall certify to the district court such portions of the record of its proceeding as the district court
may request. Notwithstanding paragraph (a) of this section, the in camera record may be transmitted to a district
court and be admissible in a civil action, subject to such protective order as the district court determines necessary,
pursuant to 28 U.S.C. 1659. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * * 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
12. Section 210.41 is revised to read as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;210.41 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Termination of investigation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Except as provided in &sect;210.21(b)(2), (c) and (d), an order of termination issued by the Commission shall constitute
a determination of the Commission under &sect;210.45(c). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
13. Section 210.42 is amended by revising paragraphs (a)(1)(i), (b), (c), and (h)(3) to read as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;210.42 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Initial determinations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a)(1)(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
On issues concerning violation of section 337.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Unless otherwise ordered by the Commission, the administrative law judge shall certify the record to the Commission
and shall file an initial determination on whether there is a violation of section 337 of the Tariff Act of 1930 no later
than 3 months before the target date set pursuant to &sect;210.51(a) if the target date is 15 months or less from the
date of institution, and no later than 4 months before the target date if the target date is more than 15 months from the
date of institution. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * * 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
On issues concerning temporary relief or forfeiture of temporary relief bonds.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Certification of the record and the disposition of an initial determination concerning a motion for temporary relief
are governed by &sect;&sect;210.65 and 210.66. The disposition of an initial determination concerning possible
forfeiture or return of a complainant's temporary relief bond, in whole or in part, is governed by &sect;210.70. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
On other matters.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The administrative law judge shall grant the following types of motions by issuing an initial determination or shall
deny them by issuing an order: a motion to amend the complaint or notice of investigation pursuant to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;210.14(b); a motion for a finding of default pursuant to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;210.16; a motion for summary determination pursuant to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;210.18; a motion for intervention pursuant to &sect;210.19; a motion for termination pursuant to &sect;210.21;
a motion to suspend an investigation pursuant to &sect;210.23; a motion for forfeiture or return of respondents'
bonds pursuant to &sect;210.50(d); a motion to set a target date exceeding 15 months pursuant to &sect;210.51(a);
or a motion for forfeiture or return of a complainant's temporary relief bond pursuant to &sect;210.70. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * * 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(h) *&blank;*&blank;* 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) An initial determination filed pursuant to &sect;210.42(c) shall become the determination of the Commission
30 days after the date of service of the initial determination, except as provided in paragraph (h)(5) of this section,
&sect;210.50(d)(3) and &sect;210.70(c), unless the Commission, within 30 days after the date of such service shall
have ordered review of the initial determination or certain issues therein or by order has changed the effective date
of the initial determination. 
