<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00051 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00010 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=69 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=52 g=1 f=1 -->

<CFRNO>33 CFR Part 117</CFRNO>
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=41 g=1 f=1 -->

<RINDOCK>[CGD05&hyph;94&hyph;103]</RINDOCK>
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=91 g=1 f=1 -->

<RINDOCK>RIN 2115&hyph;AE47</RINDOCK>
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=55 g=1 f=1 -->
Drawbridge Operation Regulations; Atlantic Intracoastal Waterway, Chesapeake, VA
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<AGENCY>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
AGENCY: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
Coast Guard, DOT.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</AGENCY>
<ACTION>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
ACTION: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
Interim rule with request for comments.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=59 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</ACTION>
<SUMMARY>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
SUMMARY: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
At the request of the City of Chesapeake, Virginia the Coast Guard is changing the regulations that govern the operation
of the drawbridge across the Southern Branch of the Elizabeth River, Atlantic Intracoastal Waterway, mile 5.8, at
Chesapeake, Virginia, by limiting bridge openings during the morning and evening rush hours. This rule will allow
commercial cargo vessels, tugs, and tugs with tows passage through the bridge during morning and evening rush hours,
provided a 2-hour advance notice is given to the Gilmerton Bridge. This rule also includes a provision that allows
public vessels of the United States, vessels in distress, commercial vessels carrying liquefied flammable gas or
other harmful substances, and commercial or public vessels assisting in an emergency situation passage through
the bridge at any time. All other commercial and recreational vessel traffic will be denied draw openings during the
morning and evening rush hours. The changes to these regulations are, to the extent practical and feasible, intended
to provide for regularly scheduled drawbridge openings to help reduce motor vehicle traffic delays and congestion
on the roads and highways linked by this drawbridge while providing for the reasonable needs of navigation.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</SUMMARY>
<DATE>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
DATES: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
This interim rule is effective December 30, 1994. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Comments must be received on or before March 30, 1995.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</DATE>
<ADDRESS>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
ADDRESSES: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
Comments may be mailed to Commander (ob), Fifth Coast Guard District, 431 Crawford Street, Portsmouth, Virginia
23704&hyph;5004, or may be delivered to Room 109 at the same address between 8 a.m. and 4 p.m., Monday through Friday,
except Federal holidays. The telephone number is (804) 398&hyph;6222. Comments will become part of this docket and
will be available for inspection at Room 109, Fifth Coast Guard District.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</ADDRESS>
<FURTHER>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
FOR FURTHER INFORMATION CONTACT:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
Ann B. Deaton, Bridge Administrator, Fifth Coast Guard District, at (804) 398&hyph;6222.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FURTHER>
<SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=2 -->
SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Request for Comments
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=2 -->
The Coast Guard encourages interested persons to participate in this rulemaking by submitting written data, views,
or arguments. Persons submitting comments should include their names and addresses, identify this rulemaking (CGD05&hyph;94&hyph;103)
and the specific section of this rule to which each comment applies, and give the reason for each comment. The Coast
Guard requests that all comments and attachments be submitted in an unbound format suitable for copying and electronic
filing. If not practical, a second copy of any bound material is requested. Persons wanting acknowledgment of receipt
of comments should enclose a stamped, self-addressed postcard or envelope.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The Coast Guard will consider all comments received during the comment period. It may change this rule in view of the
comments.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The Coast Guard plans no public hearing. Persons may request a public hearing by writing to the Commander (ob) at the
address under ADDRESSES
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The request should include reasons why a hearing would be beneficial. If it determines that the opportunity for oral
presentations will aid this rulemaking, the Coast Guard will hold a public hearing at a time and place announced by
a later notice in the 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Federal Register.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
Drafting information: The principal persons involved in drafting this document are Linda L. Gilliam, Project Manager,
Bridge Section, and LCDR C. A. Abel, Project Counsel, Fifth Coast Guard District Legal Office. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00052 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00010 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Background and Purpose
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The City of Chesapeake, Virginia has requested that openings of the Gilmerton Highway drawbridge across the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Southern Branch of the Elizabeth River, Atlantic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Intracoastal Waterway, mile 5.8, at Chesapeake, Virginia, be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limited during the morning and evening rush hours. This 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
would help reduce highway traffic congestion problems and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
address public safety and welfare concerns associated with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
frequent bridge openings caused by recreational and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
commercial boat traffic. The City of Chesapeake's request 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is based on the increase in highway traffic crossing the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Gilmerton Bridge occurring as a result of the emergency 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
closing to highway traffic of the Jordan Bridge located 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
downriver at mile 2.8. When the Jordan Bridge experienced a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sudden mechanical malfunction on May 10, 1994, this vertical 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
lift bridge was raised to the fully opened to river traffic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
position in order not to block use of the waterway by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
heavy commercial and recreational traffic routinely 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transitting the Intracoastal Waterway. As a result of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
locking the bridge in the open position until further 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
notice, the highway traffic that had been using the Jordan 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Bridge was diverted to the Gilmerton Bridge. The increase 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in highway congestion and lengthy delays across the bridge 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
caused by the Jordan Bridge's closure, coupled with random, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
non-scheduled drawbridge openings for the many commercial 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and recreational vessels using the Intracoastal Waterway 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in this area warrants the need to change the operating schedule 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for this bridge.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Currently, the drawbridge opens on demand, 24-hours a day, seven-days a week. This rule will limit bridge openings
between the hours of 6:30 a.m. to 8 a.m. and from 3:30 p.m. to 5 p.m., Monday through Friday, except Federal holidays.
Commercial cargo vessels, tugs, and tugs with tows will be allowed passage through the bridge during the morning and
evening rush hours, provided a 2-hour advance notice is given to the Gilmerton Bridge.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Public vessels of the United States, vessels in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
distress, commercial vessels carrying liquefied flammable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gas or other harmful substances, and commercial or public 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vessels assisting in an emergency situation will be allowed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
passage through the bridge at any time. Recreational 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vessels and all other commercial vessels will not be allowed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
passage through the bridge during the morning and evening 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rush hours. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The decision to allow liquefied flammable gas carriers 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
access through the bridge at any time with no restrictions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
was made based on the hazards involved in shipping liquefied 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
flammable gas and to maintain safety along the Southern 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Branch of the Elizabeth River. It has been determined by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Coast Guard that since tugs and tugs with tows have no 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
place to tie up in the proximity of the bridge to wait for a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
bridge opening, it was necessary to include them in the 2-hour 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
advance notice requirement provision. Commercial cargo 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vessels, requiring high tide to transit this river also are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
included in the 2-hour advance notice requirement provision. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The Gilmerton Bridge is a vital link between the cities 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of Portsmouth and Chesapeake used widely by motorists that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
work at the Norfolk Naval Shipyard, other Federal agencies 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
located within the Shipyard, as well as within Portsmouth, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and other industries and businesses in Portsmouth and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Chesapeake, Virginia. It appears the need to limit bridge 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
openings during peak rush hours far outweighs any need to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintain the Gilmerton Bridge at its present ``open on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demand'' schedule. On November 2, 1994, the Coast Guard met 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with the Hampton Roads Maritime Association to discuss 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
changing the regulations on the Gilmerton Bridge and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reasons why restricting this bridge during the morning and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
evening rush hours was necessary. The Hampton Roads 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Maritime Association considered the current condition of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Jordan Bridge and they supported the plan to regulate the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Gilmerton Bridge to accommodate the additional vehicle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
traffic being diverted from the Jordan Bridge. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00053 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00010 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Coast Guard believes these restrictions will not unduly restrict vessel passage through the bridge, as vessel
operators and the marine industry have agreed to and can plan transits around the interim schedule. Due to the unexpected
closure of the Jordan Bridge to highway traffic, the Coast Guard believes it is in the public interest to regulate the
Gilmerton Bridge; therefore, good cause exists for publishing this rule without prior notice and opportunity for
comment, and making it effective in less than the 30 days after publication normally required. This rule should be
effective immediately because it is in the overall public interest to do so, and the Coast Guard is not aware of any reasons
not to.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Regulatory Evaluation
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This rule is not a significant regulatory action under section 3(f) of Executive Order 12866 and does not require an
assessment of potential costs and benefits under section 6(a)(3) of that order. It has been exempted from review by
the Office of Management and Budget under that order. It is not significant under the regulatory policies and procedures
of the Department of Transportation (DOT) (44 FR 11040; February 26, 1979). The Coast Guard expects the economic impact
of this rule to be so minimal that a full Regulatory Evaluation under paragraph 10e of the regulatory policies and procedures
of DOT is unnecessary.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Small Entities
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Under the Regulatory Flexibility Act (5 U.S.C. 601 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
et seq.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
), the U.S. Coast Guard must consider whether the economic impact on small entities of a rule for which a general notice
of proposed rulemaking is required. ``Small entities'' include independently owned and operated small businesses
that are not dominant in their field and that otherwise qualify as ``small business concerns'' under section 3 of the
Small Business Act (15 U.S.C. 632). This rule does not require a general notice of proposed rulemaking and, therefore,
is exempt from the regulatory flexibility requirements. Although exempt, the Coast Guard has reviewed this rule
for potential impact on small entities. Because it expects the impact of this rule to be minimal, the Coast Guard certifies
under 5 U.S.C. 605(b) that this rule will not have a significant economic impact on a substantial number of small entities.
If, however, you think that your business qualifies as a small entity and that this rule will have a significant economic
impact on your business, please submit a comment (see 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=2 -->
ADDRESSES
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) explaining why you think your business qualifies and in what way and to what degree this rule will affect your business
economically.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Collection of Information
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This rule contains no collection of information requirements under the Paperwork Reduction Act (44 U.S.C. 3501 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
et seq.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Federalism
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This action has been analyzed in accordance with the principals and criteria contained in Executive Order 12612,
and it has been determined that the proposed rulemaking does not have sufficient federalism implications to warrant
the preparation of a Federalism Assessment.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Environment
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Coast Guard considered the environmental impact of this rule and concluded that under section 2.B.2.e(32)(e)
of Commandant Instruction M16475.1B, this rule is categorically excluded from further environmental documentation.
A Categorical Exclusion Determination statement has been prepared and placed in the rulemaking docket.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
List of Subjects in 33 CFR Part 117
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Bridges.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Regulations
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In consideration of the foregoing, the Coast Guard is amending Part 117 of Title 33, Code of Federal Regulations to
read as follows:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=52 g=1 f=1 -->
PART 117_DRAWBRIDGE OPERATION REGULATIONS
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
1. The authority citation for Part 117 continues to read as follows:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=4 -->
Authority:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 33 U.S.C. 499; 49 CFR 1.46; 33 CFR 1.05&hyph;1(g).
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
2. In Section 117.997, paragraphs (c), (d), (e), and (f) are redesignated as (d), (e), (f), and (g) and a new paragraph
(c) is added to read as follows:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00054 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00010 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;117.997 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Atlantic Intracoastal Waterway, South Branch of the Elizabeth River to the Albemarle and Chesapeake Canal.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(c) The draw of the Gilmerton (US13/460) bridge, mile 5.8, in Chesapeake:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Shall open on signal at any time for public vessels of the United States, vessels in distress, commercial vessels
carrying liquefied flammable gas or other harmful substances, and commercial and/or public vessels assisting in
any emergency situation.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) From 6:30 a.m. to 8 a.m. and from 3:30 p.m. to 5 p.m., Monday through Friday, except Federal holidays the bridge:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Need not open for the passage of pleasure craft or commercial vessels that do not qualify under paragraph (c)(2)(ii)
of this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Need not open for commercial cargo vessels, including tugs, and tugs with tows, unless 2 hours advance notice
has been given to the Gilmerton Bridge at (804) 545&hyph;1512.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Shall open on signal at all other times.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
