<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00062 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=94 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=69 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=50 g=1 f=1 -->


<USDEPT>LIBRARY OF CONGRESS</USDEPT>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=18 g=1 f=1 -->

<USBUREAU>Copyright Office</USBUREAU>
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=52 g=1 f=1 -->

<CFRNO>37 CFR Part 201 </CFRNO>
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=41 g=1 f=1 -->

<RINDOCK>[Docket No. RM 86&hyph;7B] </RINDOCK>
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=55 g=1 f=1 -->
Cable Compulsory License; Definition of Cable System 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<AGENCY>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
AGENCY:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 Copyright Office, Library of Congress. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</AGENCY>
<ACTION>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
ACTION:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 Amendment of cable license regulation.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=59 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</ACTION>
<SUMMARY>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
SUMMARY:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 The Copyright Office is repealing the provision of its regulations regarding the eligibility of multipoint distribution
service and multichannel multipoint distribution service operators for compulsory licensing under section 111
of the Copyright Act, and is amending other regulatory provisions necessitated by the Satellite Home Viewer Act of
1994. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</SUMMARY>
<DATE>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
EFFECTIVE DATE:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 January 1, 1995. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</DATE>
<FURTHER>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
FOR FURTHER INFORMATION CONTACT:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 Marilyn J. Kretsinger, Acting General Counsel, Copyright GC/I&amp;R, P.O. Box 70400, Southwest Station, Washington,
D.C. 20024. Telephone: (202) 707&hyph;8380. Telefax: (202) 707&hyph;8366. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FURTHER>
<SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 On October 18, 1994, the President signed into law the Satellite Home Viewer Act of 1994 (1994 Home Viewer Act). Public
Law 103&hyph;369, 108 Stat. 3477. The 1994 Home Viewer Act extends the Copyright Act's section 119 compulsory license
for satellite carriers another five years, until December 31, 1999, and amends the section 111 cable compulsory license
definitions of a ``cable system'' and the ``local service area of a primary transmitter.'' These legislative amendments
to the Copyright Act require certain changes in Subchapter A, Part 201 of the Copyright Office's regulations, 37 C.F.R.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Definition of a Cable System_Wireless Cable Systems 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The 1994 Home Viewer Act amends the definition of a ``cable system'' in the section 111 cable compulsory license to
include what are known as ``wireless'' cable systems. ``Wireless'' cable operators, which provide video retransmission
in the Multipoint Distribution Service (MDS) and the Multichannel Multipoint Distribution Service (MMDS), are
eligible for section 111 compulsory licensing for the broadcast signals that they retransmit to their subscribers.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
By clarifying the section 111(f) definition of a ``cable system'' to include ``wireless'' cable operators, the 1994
Home Viewer Act expressly overruled a prior decision of the Copyright Office that ``wireless'' cable operators did
not come within the section 111(f) definition. On January 29, 1992, the Office concluded its inquiry into the definition
of a ``cable system'' in Docket No. 86&hyph;7B and issued a regulation denying both ``wireless'' cable operators
and satellite carriers eligibility for the cable compulsory license. 57 FR 3284 (1992). This regulation added a new
subsection (k) to section 201.17 of the Office's rules, the pertinent part of which provided: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Satellite Carriers and MMDS Not Eligible 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Satellite carriers, satellite resale carriers, multipoint distribution services, and multichannel multipoint
distribution services are not eligible for the cable compulsory license based upon an interpretation of the whole
of section 111 of title 17 of the United States Code. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Subsequent to the issuance of this regulation, the Copyright Office delayed its effective date until January 1, 1995.
58 FR 40363 (July 28, 1993). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
In light of the 1994 Home Viewer Act change to the ``cable system'' definition, the Office is amending &sect;201.17(k)
to conform to the law and will treat ``wireless'' cable operators as being eligible for the cable compulsory license
since January 1, 1978, the effective date of the Copyright Act and section 111. Satellite carriers, however, continue
to remain ineligible for the section 111 license and the regulation is revised to notify satellite carriers when they
may request a refund of royalties submitted to the Copyright Office under section 111. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Local Service Area of a Primary Transmitter 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The other change to the cable compulsory license made by the 1994 Home Viewer Act is the broadening of the section 111(f)
definition of the ``local service area of a primary transmitter.'' The definition is used to determine when a broadcast
station is local or distant to a cable operator, which in turn determines whether the operator must pay a royalty fee
for that station. Effective July 1, 1994, the local service area of a broadcast station for copyright purposes also
includes the area in which the station is entitled to insist upon carriage of its signal by a cable system (i.e. its must-carry
zone), in accordance with the rules of the Federal Communications Commission in effect on September 18, 1993, and
any subsequent modification of those rules. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Satellite Carriers 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 201.11(a) and (b) are amended to reflect passage of the 1994 Home Viewer Act, including the royalty rate and
the definitional changes to section 119 of the Copyright Act. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
List of Subjects in 37 CFR Part 201 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Cable systems, satellite carriers, compulsory license. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00063 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Proposed Regulation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In consideration of the foregoing, part 201 of title 37, Code of Federal Regulations, is amended as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=52 g=1 f=1 -->
PART 201_[AMENDED] 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
1. The authority citation for part 201 is revised to read as follows: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=4 -->
Authority:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 17 U.S.C. 702.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;201.11
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
[Amended] 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
2. Section 201.11 is amended by removing ``100&hyph;667'' every place it appears and adding ``103&hyph;369''. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
3. Section 201.11(e)(6) is amended by removing ``twelve (12) cents per subscriber'' and adding ``17.5 cents per subscriber,
or in the case of syndex-proof superstations as defined in 37 CFR 258.2, 14 cents''. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
4. Section 201.11(e)(7) is amended by removing ``three (3)'' and adding ``six (6)''. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;201.17
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
[Amended]
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
5. Section 201.17(a) is amended by removing ``, as amended by Pub. L. 94&hyph;553,''. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
6. Section 201.17(b)(2) is amended in the first sentence by adding ``microwave,'' after ``cables,''; by removing
``Notices required to be recorded by this section, and the''; and by removing ``: (i) On the date of recordation with
the Copyright Office, in the case of the preparation and filing of an Initial Notice of Identity and Signal Carriage
Complement or notice of Change of Identity or Signal Carriage Complement; or (ii)''. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
6a. Section 201.17(b)(5) is amended by adding ``and Pub. L. 103&hyph;369'' at the end of the sentence before the period.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
7. Section 201.17(h)(1)(i) is amended by removing ``308.2(a)'' and adding ``256.2(a)''. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
7a. Section 201.17 in paragraphs (h)(1)(iii), (h)(2)(i), and (h)(3)(iii)(A) is amended by removing ``308.2(c)''
and adding ``256.2(c)''. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
7b. Section 201.17(h)(9) is amended by removing ``308(c)(2)'' and adding ``308.2(c)''. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
8. Section 201.17(k) is revised to read as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;201.17
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Statements of account covering compulsory licenses for secondary transmissions by cable systems.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(k) Satellite carriers not eligible. Satellite carriers and satellite resale carriers are not eligible for the cable
compulsory license based upon an interpretation of the whole of section 111 of title 17 of the United States Code. Any
such entity who paid copyright royalties into the Copyright Office in an attempt to comply with 17 U.S.C. 111 may obtain
a refund of such royalties by submitting a written request to the Chief, Licensing Division, Copyright Office, Library
of Congress, Washington DC 20557 no later than March 1, 1995. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
Dated: December 22, 1994. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

