<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00068 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00013 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=52 g=1 f=1 -->
PART 95&hyph;MANDATORY PATENT LICENSES 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=20 g=1 f=1 -->
Sec. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=26 g=1 f=1 -->
95.1&blank;Definitions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
95.2&blank;Petition for mandatory license. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
95.3&blank;Findings prior to application to Attorney General. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
95.4&blank;Limitations on mandatory licenses. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=4 -->
Authority:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 42 U.S.C. 7609; Sec. 104, Pub. L. 103&hyph;182, 107 Stat. 2057, 2064. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;95.1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Definitions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) As used in this part, all terms not defined in this section shall have the meaning given them by the Act. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Act
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the Clean Air Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. &sect;&sect;7401&hyph;7671). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Agency 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the Environmental Protection Agency. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Administrator 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the Administrator of the Environmental Protection Agency. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;95.2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Petition for mandatory license.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) Any party required to comply with sections 111, 112 or 202 of the Act (42 U.S.C. 7411, 7412 or 7521) may petition to
the Administrator for a mandatory patent license pursuant to section 308 of the Act (42 U.S.C. 7608), under a patent
that the petitioner maintains is necessary to enable the petitioner to comply with Sections 111, 112 or 202 of the Act.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b)(1) Each petition shall be signed by the petitioner and shall state the petitioner's name and address. If the petitioner
is a corporation, the petition shall be signed by an authorized officer of the corporation, and the petition shall
indicate the state of incorporation. Where the petitioner elects to be represented by counsel, a signed notice to
that effect shall be included with the petition at the time of filing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Each petition shall include a copy of the patent under which a mandatory patent license is sought. The petition
shall identify all current owners of the patent and shall include a copy of all assignment documents relevant to the
patent that are available from the United States Patent and Trademark Office. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Each petition must identify any person whose interest the petitioner believes may be affected by the grant of the
license to which the petition is directed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Each petition must contain a concise statement of all of the essential facts upon which it is based. No particular
form of statement is required. Each petition shall be verified by the petitioner or by the person having the best knowledge
of such facts. In the case of facts stated on information and belief, the source of such information and grounds of belief
shall be given. The statement of facts shall include the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) An identification of the provisions of the Act and/or regulations thereunder that the petitioner maintains petitioner
will be able to comply with if the petitioner is granted the patent license that is the subject of the petition; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) An identification of the nature and purpose of the petitioner's intended use of the patent license; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) An explanation of the relationship between the patented technology and the activities to which petitioner
proposes to apply the patented technology, including an estimate of the effect on such activities stemming from the
grant or denial of the patent license; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) A summary of facts demonstrating that the patent under which a mandatory patent license is sought is being used
or is intended for public or commercial use; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00069 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00013 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(v) An explanation of why a mandatory patent license is necessary for the petitioner to comply with the requirements
of sections 111, 112 or 202 of the Act, and why the patented technology is not otherwise available; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) An explanation of why there are no other reasonable alternatives for accomplishing compliance with sections
111, 112 or 202 of the Act; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) An explanation of why the unavailability of a mandatory patent license may result in a substantial lessening
of competition or a tendency to create a monopoly in any line of commerce in any section of the United States; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(viii) A summary of efforts made by the petitioner to obtain a patent license from the owner of the patent, including
the terms and conditions of any patent license proposed by petitioner to the patent owner; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ix) The terms, if any, on which the owner of the patent has proposed to grant the petitioner a patent license. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) Each petition shall include a proposed patent license that states all of the terms and conditions that the petitioner
proposes for the patent license. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) Petitions shall be addressed to the Assistant Administrator for Air and Radiation, Mail Code 6101, U.S. Environmental
Protection Agency, Washington, DC 20460. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) Petitions that do not include all of the information required in paragraph (b) of this section shall be returned
to the petitioner. The petitioner may supplement the petition and resubmit the petition. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) If the Administrator, or the Administrator's designee, finds that the criteria in &sect;95.3 are not met, or otherwise
decides to deny the petition, a denial of the petition shall be sent to the petitioner, along with an explanation of
the reasons for the denial. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) If the Administrator, or the Administrator's designee, finds that the criteria in &sect;95.3 are met and decides
to apply to the Attorney General for a patent license under section 308 of the Act, notice of such application shall
be given to the petitioner, along with a copy of the application sent to the Attorney General. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;95.3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Findings prior to application to Attorney General.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Administrator, or the Administrator's designee, may apply to the Attorney General for a mandatory patent license
pursuant to section 308 of the Act (42 U.S.C. 7608) either in response to a petition under &sect;95.2 or on the Administrator's
or designee's own initiative, only after expressly finding that each one of the following mandatory criteria is met:

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(a) The application is for a patent license covering no more than one patent; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) The party to whom the proposed patent license is to be granted has presented the Administrator or designee with
evidence that such party has made reasonable efforts to obtain a patent license from the patent owner with terms similar
to the license terms to be proposed in the application to the Attorney General; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) The patent under which a patent license is sought in the application to the Attorney General is being used or is intended
for public or commercial use; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) The mandatory patent license is necessary for a party to comply with the requirements of sections 111, 112 or 202
of the Act (42 U.S.C. 7411, 7412 or 7521); 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00070 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00013 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(e) The patented technology is not otherwise reasonably available, and there are no other reasonable alternatives
for accomplishing compliance with sections 111, 112 or 202 of the Act (42 U.S.C. 7411, 7412 or 7521); and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(f) The unavailability of a mandatory patent license may result in a substantial lessening of competition or a tendency
to create a monopoly in any line of commerce in any section of the United States. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;95.4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Limitations on mandatory licenses 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) If the Administrator, or the Administrator's designee, decides to apply to the Attorney General for a mandatory
patent license in accordance with &sect;95.3, the application shall include a proposed patent license with the following
limitations: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) The scope and duration of the patent license shall be limited to that necessary to permit the proposed licensee
to comply with the requirements the Act; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The patent license shall be nonexclusive; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) The patent license shall be non-assignable, except with that part of the enterprise or goodwill that enjoys the
license; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) The patent license shall be for use of the licensed technology in the United States only; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) The patent license shall extend only to those uses necessary to enable the licensee to comply with sections 111,
112 or 202 of the Act (42 U.S.C. 7411, 7412 or 7521); 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) The patent license shall provide for termination, subject to adequate protections of the legitimate interests
of the licensed party, when the circumstances that made the compulsory patent license necessary cease to exist and
are unlikely to recur; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) The patent license shall provide for adequate remuneration that takes into account the economic value of the license.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) The Administrator, or the Administrator's designee, may decide as appropriate to include additional conditions,
terms or limitations on the scope of the patent license for which application is made to the Attorney General. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 03 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

