<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rule 102(e) of Regulation S&hyph;T. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Rule 102(e) of Regulation S&hyph;T has been amended to clarify the requirement that, after a date three years after
its phase-in date, a registered investment company or business development company may incorporate by reference
only documents filed electronically. Specifically, the amendments clarify that the exemption in the rule for documents
filed in paper pursuant to a hardship exemption would be applicable only if any required confirming copy has been submitted.
The rules also now provide that an exhibit, filed in paper, to Form N&hyph;SAR
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
59
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 may be incorporated by reference into another Form N&hyph;SAR filing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
59
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
17 CFR 274.101. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rule 302(b) of Regulation S&hyph;T. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In order to avoid any filer misunderstanding of the current requirement to retain a manually signed signature page
or other signature authentication document, the Commission is clarifying the rule to specifically require a manual
signature with respect to each signatory to the electronic filing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
New Rule 302(c) of Regulation S&hyph;T. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
As proposed, Commission rules no longer will require manual signatures on the paper copies of electronic filings
required to be furnished by filers to national securities exchanges and national securities associations.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
60
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
60
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
For example, Exchange Act Rule 12b&hyph;11 [17 CFR 240.12b&hyph;11] requires that a manually signed copy of Exchange
Act reports be filed with each exchange upon which the registrant's securities are registered. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
New Rules 303(a)(3) and (4) of Regulation S&hyph;T. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The following are added to the list of documents that may not be incorporated by reference, consistent with other rule
provisions
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
61
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 and current staff interpretations: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
61
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=3 -->
See 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
revised Rule 102(e) of Regulation S&hyph;T [17 CFR 232.102(e)]. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For a registered investment company or a business development company making electronic submissions more than three
years after its phase-in date, a document which has not been filed in electronic format, unless the document has been
filed in paper pursuant to a hardship exemption and any required confirming copy has been submitted or the document
is an exhibit, filed in paper, to Form N&hyph;SAR, and is being incorporated by reference into another Form N&hyph;SAR
filing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
For investment company filings, any Financial Data Schedule required under Securities Act Rule 483.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
62
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
62
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
17 CFR 230.483. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rule 304(a) of Regulation S&hyph;T. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Under the amended rules, descriptions of omitted graphic and image material will be allowed to be placed either in
the text of an electronic filing where the omission occurs or in an appendix thereto, at the option of the filer. Registrants
no longer will be required to list all omitted material in an appendix to the filing. Descriptions should be provided
in narrative or tabular format, as appropriate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rule 304(d) of Regulation S&hyph;T. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Phased-in registrants subject to the requirement to furnish a stock performance comparison graph in their proxy
statements pursuant to Item 402(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
l
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of Regulation S&hyph;K
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
63
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 will be required to satisfy that obligation in their electronic filing in the same manner as applicable to other types
of omitted charts or graphs, that is, by describing the omitted performance graph by presenting the graph's data points
in tabular form.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
64
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The requirement to furnish a paper copy of the performance graph to the Branch Chief in the Division of Corporation
Finance responsible for the review of the registrant's filings is retained, in order to allow the staff to continue
monitoring information as distributed to investors.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
65
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 As proposed, the option to file the graph in paper under cover of Form SE
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
66
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is eliminated to prevent the possibility of an incomplete electronic presentation to the reader without reference
to the Form SE. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
63
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
17 CFR 229.402
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=3 -->
l. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=3 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
64
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=3 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=3 -->
See 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
letter from Mauri L. Osheroff, Associate Director, Regulatory Policy, Division of Corporation Finance, dated November
16, 1993, for an example of how the performance graph may be presented in tabular form in the proxy statement. This letter
is available through the EDGAR Bulletin Board. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
65
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
The previous requirement was found in Rule 304(d)(2) of Regulation S&hyph;T [17 CFR 232.304(d)(2)]. It now is incorporated
into paragraph (d) of that section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
66
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
Rule 304(d)(1) of Regulation S&hyph;T [17 CFR 232.304(d)(1)]. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
New Rule 311(b) of Regulation S&hyph;T. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The rule governing filing of exhibits in paper under cover of Form SE has been amended as proposed to provide that exhibits
to a Commission schedule filed pursuant to Section 13 or 14(d) of the Exchange Act may be filed in paper under cover of
Form SE where such exhibits previously were filed in paper (either before becoming subject to mandated electronic
filing or pursuant to a hardship exemption) and are required to be refiled pursuant to the schedule's general instructions.
In the past, such documents were required to be filed in electronic format along with the schedule to which they relate,
absent a hardship exemption.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
67
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
67
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
For example, where an issuer delivers its Form 10&hyph;K with its Schedule 13E&hyph;4 [17 CFR 240.13e&hyph;101]
in connection with its issuer tender offer proposal, the Form 10&hyph;K must be filed as an exhibit to the schedule,
notwithstanding the fact that it previously had been filed with the Commission. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=3 -->
See
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
 Item 9 of Schedule 13E&hyph;4. Under prior rules, the Form 10&hyph;K was required to be filed electronically as an
exhibit, even if it originally had been filed in paper. Under the rules adopted today, the exhibit will continue to
be required, but it may be filed in paper under cover of Form SE if it originally had been filed in paper. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00102 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00019 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
New Rule 311(c) of Regulation S&hyph;T. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Under the amended rules, insurance companies that file information included in their annual statements provided
to state insurance regulators (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
i.e.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
, Schedules O and P)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
68
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 as exhibits to their Forms 10&hyph;K will be allowed to file such documents in paper under cover of Form SE because of
difficulties in translating them into a format compatible with EDGAR.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
69
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
68
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=3 -->
See
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
 Item 601(b)(28) of Regulations S&hyph;K and &blank;&blank;
<!-- PJG 0034 unknown -->
S&hyph;B [17 CFR 229.601(b)(28) and 228.601(b)(28), respectively]. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
69
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
Since April 1993, the staff, via delegated authority, has granted requests for continuing hardship exemptions (Rule
202 of Regulation S&hyph;T [17 CFR 232.202]) for this type of document for a period of one year. Hardship exemptions
no longer need be obtained with respect to these documents. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rule 311(d) of Regulation S&hyph;T. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The revisions also codify the staff's interpretation that a Financial Data Schedule is not among those exhibits to
Form N&hyph;SAR that an investment company may submit in paper under cover of Form SE. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rules 901(a) and 902(a) of Regulation S&hyph;T. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
As proposed, a note has been added to Rules 901 and 902 of Regulation S&hyph;T to make it clear that registrants become
subject to mandated electronic filing upon their phase-in date and all subsequent filings must be made electronically,
even filings made with respect to transactions that commenced prior to, and are in process, at the time a registrant
is phased in.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
70
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The note to Rule 902(a) also clarifies the limited exception for definitive filings by investment companies under
Securities Act Rule 497. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
70
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
Of course, under Rule 101(a)(1)(iii) of Regulation S&hyph;T, a registrant may file its Form &blank;&blank;
<!-- PJG 0034 unknown -->
10&hyph;K or Form 10&hyph;KSB in paper if it is the first document filed with the Commission on or following its phase-in
date. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rule 901(c)(4) of Regulation S&hyph;T. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A note has been added to Rule 901 of Regulation S&hyph;T explaining that while entities subject to mandated electronic
filing generally may choose to electronically file Schedules 13D
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
71
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 and 13G
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
72
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 with respect to a paper filer, domestic electronic filers are restricted from doing so with respect to foreign private
issuers because EDGAR currently requires an Internal Revenue Service tax identification number to be inserted for
the subject company as a prerequisite to acceptance of the filing. It is anticipated that the EDGAR system will be modified
in the future to process such filings, but until that time, they should be filed in paper.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
73
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
71
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
17 CFR 240.13d&hyph;101. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
72
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
17 CFR 240.13d&hyph;102. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
73
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
Questions relating to electronic filing of Schedules 13D or 13G with respect to foreign private issuers should be
directed to Sylvia J. Reis, Assistant Director, CF&hyph;EDGAR Policy, Division of Corporation Finance, at (202)
942&hyph;2940. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00103 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00019 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rules 901(d) and 902(g) of Regulation S&hyph;T.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Since mandated electronic filing began in April 1993, filers have been required to furnish to the Commission a paper
copy of each electronic filing made during the first year following phase-in. This rule was adopted to implement Section
35A(d)(3) of the Exchange Act.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
74
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Since its proposal in 1992, filers have characterized the requirement as burdensome. In response, the Commission
proposed reducing the paper submission requirement so that filers could satisfy their paper copy obligations by
furnishing a paper copy of their first electronic filing only. Four commenters addressed the issue. Three supported
the reduction, characterizing the paper submission requirement as ``wasteful'' and ``unnecessary.'' One commenter
argued that the format of electronic filings is not as desirable to read as copies of paper documents, implying that
electronic filings are not suitable alternatives to paper filings. While it is true that electronic filings often
are not as aesthetically pleasing as typeset paper versions, the content of the filing, not its typeface, is what is
of interest to investors. Furthermore, this argument carries little weight against reducing the paper copy requirement,
since filers may satisfy such requirement by furnishing a paper printout of the electronic filing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
74
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
15 U.S.C. 78
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=3 -->
ll
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
(d)(3). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In light of the comments to the proposal, and in connection with the six-month evaluation of the EDGAR system, the Commission
has reviewed the paper copy requirement and procedures. As stated in the report, the EDGAR system is reliable, provides
a suitable alternative to written and printed filings, and provides information as effectively and efficiently
for filers, users and disseminators as the written or printed counterpart.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
75
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Consequently, the requirement has been modified, as proposed, to require new electronic filers to furnish to the
Commission one paper copy of their first electronic filing only.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
76
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Pursuant to a commenter's suggestion, the paper copy rule also is being clarified to state that persons making third
party filings, such as proxy materials or beneficial ownership reports, with respect to an electronic registrant
also are required to submit a paper copy with their first electronic filing only. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
75
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=3 -->
See
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
 Exchange Act Section 35A(d)(3)(B) [15 U.S.C. 78
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=3 -->
ll
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
(d)(3)(B)], which permits a reduction of the paper copy requirement if these elements are established. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
76
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
The requirement to place a legend on the top of the paper copy has been modified and retained; the rules also have been
modified to require the copy to be sent to the Commission's Operations Center in Alexandria, Virginia, as is currently
the practice. All filers that have submitted a paper copy of at least one electronic filing before the effective date
of this amendment may cease furnishing paper copies of electronic filings made on or after the effective date. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The Commission solicited comment about whether the six business day period for submission of the paper copy should
be shortened or lengthened. Commenters did not feel strongly about this issue; consequently, no time period changes
have been adopted. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rule 902(e) of Regulation S&hyph;T.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The amendments clarify the limited exception contained in Rule 902(e) of Regulation S&hyph;T
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
77
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 for definitive filings by investment companies under Rule 497 of the Securities Act, to mandated electronic filing.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
77
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
17 CFR 232.902(e). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00104 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00019 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
B. Changes to Item 601 of Regulations S&hyph;K and S&hyph;B 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Item 601 of Regulations S&hyph;K and S&hyph;B, which govern the filing of exhibits, including the new Financial Data
Schedule, are amended as described below. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;The exhibit tables of Regulations S&hyph;K and S&hyph;B have been amended as proposed to indicate that charter
documents are to be filed with quarterly reports on Forms 10&hyph;Q
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
78
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 and 10&hyph;QSB
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
79
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 pursuant to paragraph (b)(3) of Regulations S&hyph;K
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
80
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 and S&hyph;B
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
81
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 if such documents had been amended during the reporting period, thereby reflecting the requirements of Item 601(a)(4)
of Regulations S&hyph;B and S&hyph;K.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
82
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
78
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
17 CFR 249.308a. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
79
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
17 CFR 249.308b. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
80
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
17 CFR 229.601(b)(3). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
81
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
17 CFR 228.601(b)(3). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
82
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
17 CFR 228.601(a)(4) and 17 CFR 229.601(a)(4), respectively. Revised exhibit table of Item 601 of Regulations S&hyph;K
and S&hyph;B. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;Item 601 of Regulations S&hyph;K and S&hyph;B has been amended to state that if an instrument defining the rights
of security holders is in the form of a certificate, the text appearing on the certificate must be reproduced in an electronic
filing, together with a description of any other graphic and image material appearing on the certificate.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
83
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
83
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
Instruction to Item 601(b)(4) of Regulations S&hyph;K and S&hyph;B [17 CFR 229.601(b)(4) and 17 CFR 228.601(b)(4),
respectively]. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;Item 601(b)(10) of Regulations S&hyph;K and S&hyph;B has been amended to clarify that a material contract
that becomes effective or that is executed during the reporting period reflected by an annual or quarterly report
must be filed as an exhibit to the periodic report filed for the corresponding period.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
84
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The amended rules also make it clear that only new material contracts must be filed with quarterly reports; Forms 10&hyph;Q
and 10&hyph;QSB, unlike Forms 10&hyph;K and 10&hyph;KSB, do not require a list of all material contracts. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
84
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
Instruction 2 to Item 601(b)(10) to Regulations S&hyph;K and S&hyph;B [17 CFR 229.601(b)(10) and 17 CFR 228.601(b)(10),
respectively]. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
&bull;Applications filed for the purpose of determining the eligibility of a person designated as trustee for debt
securities registered under the Securities Act that are eligible to be issued, offered, or sold on a delayed basis
by or on behalf of the registrant, pursuant to Section 305(b)(2) of the Trust Indenture Act,
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
85
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 will now be required to be filed separately in the manner prescribed by the EDGAR Filer Manual.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
86
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Prior to this amendment, such filings were required to be filed as an exhibit to a post-effective amendment to the registration
statement to which the application relates. This change is intended to provide expedited processing of such filings.
Of course, the general procedure requiring all other trust indenture eligibility applications on Form T&hyph;1
and T&hyph;2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

