13. By amending &sect;232.102 by revising paragraphs (a) and (e), to read as follows:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;232.102 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Exhibits.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) Exhibits to an electronic filing that have not previously been filed with the Commission shall be filed in electronic
format, absent a hardship exemption. Previously filed exhibits, whether in paper or electronic format, may be incorporated
by reference into an electronic filing to the extent permitted by Rule 24 of the Commission's Rules of Practice (&sect;201.24
of this chapter), Rule 411 under the Securities Act (&sect;230.411 of this chapter), Rule 12b&hyph;23 or 12b&hyph;32
under the Exchange Act (&sect;240.12b&hyph;23 or &sect;240.12b&hyph;32 of this chapter), Rule 22 under the Public
Utility Holding Company Act (&sect;250.22 of this chapter), Rules 0&hyph;4, 8b&hyph;23, and 8b&hyph;32 under the
Investment Company Act (&sect;270.0&hyph;4, &sect;270.8b&hyph;23 and &sect;270.8b&hyph;32 of this chapter)
and Rule 303 of Regulation S&hyph;T (&sect;232.303). An electronic filer may, at its option, restate in electronic
format an exhibit incorporated by reference that originally was filed in paper format.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=4 -->
Note to paragraph a: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
Exhibits to a Commission schedule filed pursuant to Section 13 or 14(d) of the Exchange Act may be filed in paper under
cover of Form SE where such exhibits previously were filed in paper (prior to a registrant's becoming subject to mandated
electronic filing or pursuant to a hardship exemption) and are required to be refiled pursuant to the schedule's general
instructions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
See 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
Rule 311(b) of Regulation S&hyph;T (17 CFR 232.311(b)).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(e) Notwithstanding the provisions of paragraphs (a) through (d) of this section, after the date which is three years
following a registrant's phase-in date, any incorporation by reference by a registered investment company or a business
development company shall relate only to documents which have been filed in electronic format, unless:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) The document has been filed in paper pursuant to a hardship exemption (&sect;&sect;232.201 and 232.202 of this
chapter) and any required confirming copy has been submitted or
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The document is an exhibit, filed in paper in accordance with applicable rules, to Form N&hyph;SAR being incorporated
by reference only into another Form N&hyph;SAR filing.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
14. By amending &sect;232.302 by revising paragraph (b) and adding paragraph (c), to read as follows:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;232.302 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Signatures.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(b) Each signatory to an electronic filing shall manually sign a signature page or other document authenticating,
acknowledging or otherwise adopting his or her signature that appears in typed form within the electronic filing.
Such document shall be executed before or at the time the electronic filing is made and shall be retained by the filer
for a period of five years. Upon request, an electronic filer shall furnish to the Commission or its staff a copy of any
or all documents retained pursuant to this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) Where the Commission's rules require a registrant to furnish to a national securities exchange or national securities
association paper copies of a document filed with the Commission in electronic format, signatures to such paper copies
may be in typed form.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941230-0-00112 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941230-0-00019 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4700 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
15. By amending &sect;232.303 by adding paragraphs (a)(3) and (a)(4) to read as follows:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;232.303 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Incorporation by reference.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) *&blank;*&blank;*
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) For a registered investment company or a business development company making an electronic submission more than
three years after its phase-in date, documents that have not been filed in electronic format, unless:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The document has been filed in paper pursuant to a hardship exemption (&sect;&sect;232.201 and 232.202 of this
chapter) and any required confirming copy has been submitted or
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The document is an exhibit, filed in paper in accordance with applicable rules, to Form N&hyph;SAR being incorporated
by reference into another Form N&hyph;SAR filing.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Any Financial Data Schedule required under Rule 483 under the Securities Act of 1933 (&sect;230.483 of this chapter).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
16. By amending &sect;232.304 by revising paragraphs (a) and (d) to read as follows:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;232.304 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Graphic and image material.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) If an electronic filing omits graphic or image material included in the paper version of the document, the electronic
version shall include a fair and accurate narrative description or tabular representation of the omitted material.
Such descriptions or representations may be included in the text of the electronic filing where the graphic or image
material appears in the paper version, or they may be listed in an appendix to the electronic filing. Differences between
the electronic and paper versions of the document such as pagination, color, type size or style, or corporate logo
need not be described.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(d) The performance graph that is to appear in registrant proxy and information statements relating to annual meetings
of security holders (or special meetings or written consents in lieu of such meetings) at which directors will be elected,
as required by Item 402(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
l
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of Regulation S&hyph;K (&sect;229.402(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
l
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this chapter), shall be furnished to the Commission in connection with an electronic filing by presenting the
data in tabular or chart form within the electronic filing, in compliance with the formatting requirements of the
EDGAR Filer Manual. Registrants also shall submit supplementally a paper copy of the performance graph to their Branch
Chief in the Division of Corporation Finance.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
17. By amending &sect;232.306 by revising the first sentence of the note following paragraph (a), to read as follows:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;232.306 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Foreign language documents and symbols.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=4 -->
Note: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
With respect to submission of an electronic filer's latest annual budget required to be filed as Exhibit B in Form 18
(&sect;249.218 of this chapter) or as Exhibit (c) in Form 18&hyph;K (&sect;249.318 of this chapter), for foreign
governments and political subdivisions thereof, if an English version of such filer's last annual budget as presented
to its legislative body has been prepared, it shall be filed electronically. *&blank;*&blank;*
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
18. By amending &sect;232.311 by revising paragraphs (b), (c), and (d) and in paragraphs (e), (f) and (g), by replacing
the references to ``Form S&hyph;E'' with references to ``Form SE'', and in paragraph (h)(2), by revising the reference
``paragraphs (a) through (c)'' to read ``paragraphs (a) through (g)'' to read as follows:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;232.311 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Documents submitted in paper under cover of Form SE.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(b) Exhibits to a Commission schedule filed pursuant to Section 13 or 14(d) of the Exchange Act may be filed in paper
under cover of Form SE where such exhibits previously were filed in paper (prior to a registrant's becoming subject
to mandated electronic filing or pursuant to a hardship exemption) and are required to be refiled pursuant to the schedule's
general instructions.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) Exhibits consisting of all or portions of an annual statement provided to state insurance regulators (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
e.g., 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Schedules O and P), required to be filed pursuant to Item 601(b)(28) of Regulation S&hyph;B or Regulation S&hyph;K
(&sect;228.601(b)(28) or &sect;229.601(b)(28) of this chapter, respectively), may be filed in paper under cover
of Form SE.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) Exhibits to Form N&hyph;SAR (&sect;274.101 of this chapter), other than the Financial Data Schedule required
under Rule 483 under the Securities Act of 1933 (&sect;230.483 of this chapter), may be filed in paper under cover of
Form SE.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
19. By amending &sect;232.901 by adding a note to paragraph (a), by adding a note to paragraph (c)(4), by revising the
heading and introductory text of paragraph (d), and by revising paragraph (d)(2), to read as follows:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;232.901 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Division of Corporation Finance EDGAR Transition.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) *&blank;*&blank;*
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=4 -->
Note to paragraph (a): 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
Registrants become subject to mandated electronic filing on their phase-in date. Consequently, all documents required
to be filed in electronic format pursuant to Rule 101 of Regulation S&hyph;T (&sect;232.101) filed on or after a registrant's
phase-in date must be filed electronically, absent a hardship exemption, even if the transaction to which a filing
relates was commenced in paper before the phase-in date and is still in process on the registrant's phase-in date.

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
See 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
Rule 101(a)(1)(iii) of Regulation S&hyph;T, that provides for optional paper filing of a Form 10&hyph;K or 10&hyph;KSB
if it is the first document filed after a registrant's phase-in date.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(c) *&blank;*&blank;*
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) *&blank;*&blank;* 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=4 -->
Note to paragraph (c)(4): 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
While companies subject to mandated electronic filing generally may choose to electronically file Schedules 13D
and 13G with respect to a paper filer, domestic electronic filers are restricted from doing so with respect to foreign
private issuers because EDGAR currently requires an IRS tax identification number to be inserted for the subject
company as a prerequisite to acceptance of the filing. Such filings should be made in paper until the EDGAR system is
modified to process them electronically.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=37 g=1 f=1 -->
* * * * *
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

